>> title: Sesame Chicken
>> category: Stir-Fries
>> tags: chicken, sesame, chinese, deep-fry, wok
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: sesame chicken, honey sesame chicken, 芝麻雞, zhi ma ji
>> pairs-with: egg-fried-rice
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — the double fry cooks it and crisps it, and neither leg can cover for the other in a single pass
>> washing-up: the wok, a bowl to velvet in, a dish to dredge in, a rack to drain on, a bowl for the glaze

>> step: velvet, rest 30 min
Toss @chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; boneless, cut in 1-in pieces) with @egg white{1}, @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, and @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, then ~rest{30%min} in the fridge.

>> step: dredge dry, shake off the loose
Dredge @&(~1)velveted chicken{} in @cornstarch{3/4%cup}(90 g), piece by piece, shaking off what does not cling.

>> step: fry 350°F 5 min, again at 375°F 2 min
Fry @&(~1)coated chicken{} in @peanut oil{4%cups}(950 mL) in two batches at 350°F (175°C) for ~fry{5%min}, rest them on a rack, then return every piece to the oil at 375°F (190°C) for ~fry{2%min}.

>> step: stir the glaze smooth
Stir @chicken stock{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @dark soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @rice vinegar{1%Tbs}, @toasted sesame oil{1%Tbs}, and @cornstarch{2%tsp} smooth in a bowl.

>> step: simmer the aromatics 1 min
Simmer @&(~1)glaze{} with @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @fresh ginger{2%tsp}(grated) in a #wok{} for ~simmer{1%min}, until it is glossy and coats a spoon.

>> step: toss, scatter the seeds
Toss @&(~3)fried chicken{} through @&(~1)glaze{} off the heat and scatter @toasted sesame seeds{2%Tbs} over it.
